          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Both Halves In A Sentence",
          "text": "DNS turns a name into an address by walking a delegation hierarchy with caching; TLS turns a raw TCP socket into an authenticated, encrypted channel by walking a certificate hierarchy."
        },
